  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zend_jit_trace",
    "file": "php-src/ext/opcache/jit/zend_jit_trace.c",
    "description": "The tracing JIT's abstract-stack/register bookkeeping permits a CV that participates in the PoV's loop and mixed assignments/dimension operations to remain only partially synchronized with its in-memory zval. In particular, the post-op stack-state update and spill decisions can preserve/reset the memory type independently of the value held in a register. On trace exit/function return this produces a zval whose refcounted type tag is paired with a stale/non-pointer payload. The executor subsequently detaches the top-level symbol table and copies that malformed CV into EG(symbol_table); shutdown only exposes the corruption when zend_unclean_zval_ptr_dtor treats the payload as zend_refcounted and zend_gc_delref reads the wild address. Thus zend_gc_delref and hash destruction are victims, not the root cause.",
    "conditions": "Run the supplied PHP through the tracing-JIT harness so it is first interpreted to establish profile data, then traced/compiled, and finally executes the compiled trace. The program must retain the PoV's hot loop plus the relevant mixture of assignments/compound operations and array/dimension fetch-or-assignment expressions, causing a CV's concrete type/value to change while trace register allocation keeps the value in a register and tracks a different memory type. Leaving the trace or returning with that CV attached to the executor symbol table copies the inconsistent zval into the global symbol table. Request shutdown then dereferences its bogus refcounted pointer and crashes."
